WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.580
Before dawn, many Sikhs sit
still and repeat one word,

2
00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:07.930
over and over: Waheguru.

3
00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:10.890
Sikhs call this repeating the Name.

4
00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:14.270
The Name, Sikhs say, is more than a word.

5
00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:18.320
It stands for God's presence,
running through all creation.

6
00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:21.640
So how can repeating
one word, over and over,

7
00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:23.780
change the person who says it?

8
00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:26.960
In this mission, you'll
unpack two key words,

9
00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:30.450
nam and simran, and what each one means.

10
00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:33.760
Then you'll trace how
repetition is said to deepen,

11
00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:36.970
from the tongue to the mind, and beyond.

12
00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:42.190
Your mission: find out how repeating one
word can change the person who says it.
